      "summary": "A malformed follow-ups.json reaches gate.mjs as status problem { path, problem }, but checkGates reads only queuePath or specPath, so `gate.mjs check` (and close.mjs --feature, which calls checkGates) prints \"Joycraft gate: undefined does not parse: ... Repair undefined and tell the user.\" Reproduced in a temp project with a broken follow-ups.json (exit 2). payload/.joycraft/runtime/gate.mjs:44-55 is a coupled reader of status problems that is not in the spec's declared inputs.",
      "assumption": "Fix either side so the gate message names docs/<feature>/follow-ups.json (for example give the ledger problem a key gate renders, or render problem.path in gate.mjs), add gate.mjs as a declared input, and add a test for the gate/close message."
